# Icons

Icons are [Lucide](https://lucide.dev) SVGs, vendored one file per
icon in `app/assets/images/icons/` and rendered inline so they inherit
`currentColor` and theme automatically. There is no icon font and no
icon component.

## Using an icon

Render with `inline_svg_tag`, sized with Tailwind utilities:

```erb
<%%= inline_svg_tag "icons/search.svg", class: "size-4" %>
```

- `size-4` (16px) inside buttons, inputs, table rows and badges;
  `size-5`/`size-6` for navigation and feature icons.
- Colour comes from the parent's text colour — set
  `text-muted-foreground` (or a state token) on the wrapper, not on
  the SVG.
- Decorative icons sit next to their label and need no alt text;
  icon-only controls must carry an `aria-label` on the *control*.

## Adding an icon

1. Take the SVG from Lucide, unmodified (24×24 viewBox,
   `stroke="currentColor"`).
2. Save it as `app/assets/images/icons/<lucide-name>.svg`, keeping
   Lucide's kebab-case name (`check-circle-2.svg`, not
   `circle_check.svg`).
3. Use it via `inline_svg_tag` — no registry to update.

## Rules

- Lucide only — one icon set keeps stroke weight and corner radius
  consistent. Do not mix in another library's icons.
- An icon never appears without a meaning the user already knows:
  pair new or ambiguous icons with a visible label.
- Reuse the established pairings: `search`, `x` (dismiss),
  `check` (selected), `chevron-down` (expandable),
  `alert-triangle` (warning), `alert-circle` (critical),
  `info`, `check-circle-2` (success), `more-horizontal` (overflow).
- State-coloured icons take the same token as their component
  (`text-warning` icon inside a warning alert), driven by the
  component's CSS — not hand-set per page.
